{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1436092,
  "courseSlug": "react-native-the-practical-guide",
  "courseTitle": "React Native - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31894932",
      "title": "Reacting To User Interaction With Incoming Notifications",
      "lectureOrder": 251,
      "videoOrder": 242,
      "sourceHash": "4e0923b40373eb47f3ca901b4c136bdd8fa28170e7c25c307fed1888dd4dbfda",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.09,
          "end": 5.57,
          "en": "If you wanna listen to user interaction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.57,
          "end": 7,
          "en": "with our notifications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7,
          "end": 12,
          "en": "So, if you wanna react to a user tapping on a notification,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.21,
          "end": 15.28,
          "en": "we can also do this by adding such a event listener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.28,
          "end": 18.55,
          "en": "The name of the method that adds the listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.55,
          "end": 20.99,
          "en": "is just slightly different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.99,
          "end": 24.12,
          "en": "But still here, in this useEffect function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.12,
          "end": 27.211,
          "en": "we can call notifications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.211,
          "end": 30.544,
          "en": "addNotificationResponseReceivedListener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.51,
          "end": 36.07,
          "en": "Before, it was addNotificationReceivedListener,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.07,
          "end": 40.157,
          "en": "now it's addNotificationResponseReceivedListener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.065,
          "end": 44.28,
          "en": "And response simply means that the user responded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.28,
          "end": 47.083,
          "en": "to the notification by tapping on it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.2,
          "end": 51.82,
          "en": "Now just as for addNotificationReceivedListener,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.82,
          "end": 55.15,
          "en": "this method also wants a function as an argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.15,
          "end": 57.87,
          "en": "and this will be the event handler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.87,
          "end": 62.5,
          "en": "that will be triggered whenever a new response is received.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.5,
          "end": 65.1,
          "en": "And therefore, here we get a response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.1,
          "end": 68.14,
          "en": "which is almost the same as the notification object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.14,
          "end": 71.82300000000001,
          "en": "we got up here, but it is different in some details.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.67,
          "end": 76.41,
          "en": "So, as a start, simply console.log",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.41,
          "end": 79.57,
          "en": "NOTIFICATION RESPONSE RECIEVED here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.57,
          "end": 81.58,
          "en": "and then log the response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.58,
          "end": 84.43299999999999,
          "en": "so that we can look into it and see what's inside of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.72,
          "end": 88.96000000000001,
          "en": "Now, just as the addNotificationReceivedListener,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88.96000000000001,
          "end": 90.77,
          "en": "the addNotificationResponseReceivedListener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.05,
          "end": 94.33,
          "en": "also returns a subscription,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.33,
          "end": 98.22,
          "en": "and to avoid name clashes, I'll name this subscription1",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.22,
          "end": 99.57,
          "en": "and this one subscription2.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.83,
          "end": 104.31,
          "en": "And we should use this for cleanup as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.31,
          "end": 107.00999999999999,
          "en": "So we should call subscription2.remove",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.00999999999999,
          "end": 110.963,
          "en": "and subscription1.remove in this effect cleanup function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 112.36,
          "end": 114.09,
          "en": "With that we can give this a try.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 114.09,
          "end": 116.12299999999999,
          "en": "We can save this all and reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 117.4,
          "end": 119.84,
          "en": "And now if we try this on Android, maybe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.84,
          "end": 124.83,
          "en": "and we tap on this, we get this new notification here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.83,
          "end": 128.2,
          "en": "I also still have an old one, but we got the new one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 128.2,
          "end": 130.02,
          "en": "And if I don't tap on it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.02,
          "end": 132.59,
          "en": "then we all only got the output from before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.59,
          "end": 135.6,
          "en": "So we have the NOTIFICATION RECEIVED event handler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.6,
          "end": 138.32,
          "en": "doing its thing and logging this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.32,
          "end": 142.17000000000002,
          "en": "but we don't see NOTIFICATION RESPONSE RECIEVED",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 142.17000000000002,
          "end": 144.963,
          "en": "because we haven't tapped this item yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.14,
          "end": 148.8,
          "en": "But if I do now tap this notification,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 148.8,
          "end": 150.57999999999998,
          "en": "I am taken back to the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.57999999999998,
          "end": 153.51,
          "en": "That's the default behavior of the operating system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.51,
          "end": 156.28,
          "en": "and the device to load the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 156.28,
          "end": 158.69,
          "en": "to which the notification belongs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.69,
          "end": 163.16,
          "en": "But, we now also see NOTIFICATION RESPONSE RECEIVED",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.16,
          "end": 165.32999999999998,
          "en": "being logged here and that's coming from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.32999999999998,
          "end": 167.94,
          "en": "our second event handler function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.94,
          "end": 170.003,
          "en": "And we see this response object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171,
          "end": 172.7,
          "en": "As mentioned, it's very similar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.7,
          "end": 175.06,
          "en": "to the notification object from before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.06,
          "end": 177.29,
          "en": "but it's essentially an extra wrapper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 177.29,
          "end": 179.86,
          "en": "around the notification object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 179.86,
          "end": 184.86,
          "en": "So, in this response object we got a notification key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.76,
          "end": 189.22,
          "en": "and that notification key contains a notification object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.22,
          "end": 192.48,
          "en": "that has the same shape as the notification object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 192.48,
          "end": 195.123,
          "en": "we got here in the upper event handler function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.25,
          "end": 198.493,
          "en": "But, in addition to this notification key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 198.493,
          "end": 200.9,
          "en": "we also got this action identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 200.9,
          "end": 205.59,
          "en": "which basically holds some extra metadata, but that's it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 205.59,
          "end": 206.81,
          "en": "Other than that there still is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 206.81,
          "end": 209.07999999999998,
          "en": "all the notification data in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 209.07999999999998,
          "end": 214.07999999999998,
          "en": "And hence, we can also get our username here by diving into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 214.37,
          "end": 219.37,
          "en": "response.notification.request.content.data.username.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.78,
          "end": 223.16,
          "en": "And with that if we save this again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.16,
          "end": 224.35,
          "en": "and reload everything again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 224.35,
          "end": 227.32,
          "en": "maybe to clean up the terminal as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 227.32,
          "end": 229.48,
          "en": "If I schedule this on iOS again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 229.48,
          "end": 231.98,
          "en": "to also show that it works there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 231.98,
          "end": 234.69299999999998,
          "en": "If I then tap on this notification,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 235.57999999999998,
          "end": 237.07999999999998,
          "en": "I also see max here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 237.07999999999998,
          "end": 240.07,
          "en": "and that's being locked here by this line,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 240.07,
          "end": 242.43,
          "en": "as we can see, because we also got this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 242.43,
          "end": 245.61,
          "en": "NOTIFICATION RESPONSE RECIEVED output here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 245.61,
          "end": 249.08,
          "en": "So, the event handler works for iOS as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 249.08,
          "end": 253.43,
          "en": "And that is how we can react to incoming notifications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 253.43,
          "end": 256.9,
          "en": "and to user interaction with those notifications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 256.9,
          "end": 261,
          "en": "In this case, for the local notifications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 261,
          "end": 264.19,
          "en": "But I can already tell you for push notifications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 264.19,
          "end": 266.94,
          "en": "this code will be the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 266.94,
          "end": 269.87,
          "en": "The only thing that will change is that we will need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 269.87,
          "end": 273.71,
          "en": "to get some extra permissions and a push token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 273.71,
          "end": 276.35,
          "en": "and how we trigger the notifications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 276.35,
          "end": 278,
          "en": "that will change as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 278,
          "end": 280.76,
          "en": "But handling notifications will be the same,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 280.76,
          "end": 283.24,
          "en": "no matter if you're dealing with local",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 283.24,
          "end": 285.57,
          "en": "or with push notifications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 285.57,
          "end": 288.743,
          "en": "And here we worked on local notifications.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
